{"title":"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Construct a triangle <i>ABC</i> if the following elements are given: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/00791a4d801926dad4d68f03c0d4c73f4825ebe0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = b, AB = c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/4/784ab11348aaab6d6b36c6612ffb8861f76f602c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AMB = \\omega \\left(\\omega &lt; 90^{\\circ}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" /> where <i>M</i> is the midpoint of <i>BC</i>.  Prove that the construction has a solution if and only if \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c87281803e096a8ea36d878e2800ff7dd4677ada.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\tan{\\frac{\\omega}{2}} \\le c &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"120\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>In what case does equality hold?\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prolong BA to a point D such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c54de25bce1336bb9d2372e37934a7bdc281de1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = 2AB$\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />. Take circle through B and D such that the minor arc BD is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbc90d100c28b4217239d98e1bb608df909647f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2*\\omega$\" width=\"37\" height=\"12\" /> so that for points P on the major arc BD we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/e/17ef612be49d5505bc4d13b28453373582ae9651.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BPD = \\omega$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" />. Draw a circle with center A and radius AC, and the point of intersection of this circle and the major arc BD will be C. In general there are two possibilities for C.\n</p><p>Let X be the intersection of the arc BN and the perpendicular to the segment BN through A. For the construction to be possible we require <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/899f83a5086a84c4bb4766ab654e6eefb1065eb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX \\geqslant AC &gt; AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"133\" height=\"15\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29f51c022711c6f930cf0bb4f12746d83cffcece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AB}{AX} =  \\tan{\\frac{\\omega}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"101\" height=\"38\" />, so we get the condition in the question\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO\" title=\"1961 IMO\">1961 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1961 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017163703\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 75/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1486/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.548      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.548      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4853:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017163703 a